<details class="bu" open><summary><span class="bn">1</span><span class="bt">Enrollment, Admissions &amp; Marketing</span><span class="badge rev">BU leans revenue</span><span class="sm">2 mainly revenue, 0 mainly cost, 1 both</span></summary><div class="body"><ul class="branch root"><li class="lever rev"><div class="node"><div class="lh"><span class="ln"><i class="lno">Lever 1</i><b>Demand</b></span><span class="badge rev">▲ Mainly revenue</span></div></div><ul class="branch"><li class="leaf"><b>Applications and yield</b><span class="d">Applicants received and share of accepted students who enroll.</span></li><li class="leaf"><b>Market demand</b><span class="d">Demographic and competitive trends.</span></li><li class="leaf"><b>Reputation and positioning</b><span class="d">How we compare to competitors.</span></li></ul></li><li class="lever bal"><div class="node"><div class="lh"><span class="ln"><i class="lno">Lever 2</i><b>Net price</b></span><span class="badge bal">◆ Both</span></div></div><ul class="branch"><li class="leaf"><b>Tuition level</b><span class="d">Price relative to peers.</span></li><li class="leaf"><b>Discounting and scholarships</b><span class="d">Aid that reduces price for target students.</span></li><li class="leaf"><b>Net tuition per student</b><span class="d">What is actually collected after discounts.</span></li></ul></li><li class="lever rev"><div class="node"><div class="lh"><span class="ln"><i class="lno">Lever 3</i><b>Retention and recruitment</b></span><span class="badge rev">▲ Mainly revenue</span></div></div><ul class="branch"><li class="leaf"><b>Year-to-year continuity</b><span class="d">Students staying enrolled.</span></li><li class="leaf"><b>Recruitment channels</b><span class="d">Marketing, admissions staff and agents.</span></li><li class="leaf"><b>Conversion funnel</b><span class="d">Progress from enquiry to enrollment.</span></li></ul></li></ul><p class="q"><b>Critical questions</b> Are we losing applicants to competitors on price or on reputation? What is the net tuition per student after discounts?</p></div></details>
<details class="bu" open><summary><span class="bn">2</span><span class="bt">Teaching, Curriculum &amp; Academic Delivery</span><span class="badge rev">BU leans revenue</span><span class="sm">2 mainly revenue, 1 mainly cost, 0 both</span></summary><div class="body"><ul class="branch root"><li class="lever cost"><div class="node"><div class="lh"><span class="ln"><i class="lno">Lever 1</i><b>Capacity</b></span><span class="badge cost">▼ Mainly cost</span></div></div><ul class="branch"><li class="leaf"><b>Student-to-teacher ratio</b><span class="d">Balance of teaching capacity and cost.</span></li><li class="leaf"><b>Class size</b><span class="d">Number of students per session.</span></li><li class="leaf"><b>Classroom utilization</b><span class="d">Use of teaching space.</span></li></ul></li><li class="lever rev"><div class="node"><div class="lh"><span class="ln"><i class="lno">Lever 2</i><b>Curriculum</b></span><span class="badge rev">▲ Mainly revenue</span></div></div><ul class="branch"><li class="leaf"><b>Program mix</b><span class="d">Range of programs offered.</span></li><li class="leaf"><b>Job relevance</b><span class="d">Fit with labour market needs.</span></li><li class="leaf"><b>Delivery model</b><span class="d">In-person, online or hybrid.</span></li></ul></li><li class="lever rev"><div class="node"><div class="lh"><span class="ln"><i class="lno">Lever 3</i><b>Quality</b></span><span class="badge rev">▲ Mainly revenue</span></div></div><ul class="branch"><li class="leaf"><b>Learning outcomes</b><span class="d">What students actually learn.</span></li><li class="leaf"><b>Teaching quality</b><span class="d">Faculty effectiveness.</span></li><li class="leaf"><b>Faculty development</b><span class="d">Supporting better teaching.</span></li></ul></li></ul><p class="q"><b>Critical questions</b> Which programs are over- or under-subscribed? Is the delivery model matched to learner needs?</p></div></details>
<details class="bu" open><summary><span class="bn">3</span><span class="bt">Funding, Finance &amp; Research</span><span class="badge rev">BU leans revenue</span><span class="sm">2 mainly revenue, 1 mainly cost, 0 both</span></summary><div class="body"><ul class="branch root"><li class="lever rev"><div class="node"><div class="lh"><span class="ln"><i class="lno">Lever 1</i><b>Revenue mix</b></span><span class="badge rev">▲ Mainly revenue</span></div></div><ul class="branch"><li class="leaf"><b>Tuition vs government funding</b><span class="d">Balance between student-paid and state-paid income.</span></li><li class="leaf"><b>Philanthropy</b><span class="d">Gifts and donor support.</span></li><li class="leaf"><b>Dependency</b><span class="d">Reliance on any single source.</span></li></ul></li><li class="lever rev"><div class="node"><div class="lh"><span class="ln"><i class="lno">Lever 2</i><b>Research</b></span><span class="badge rev">▲ Mainly revenue</span></div></div><ul class="branch"><li class="leaf"><b>Grants and contracts</b><span class="d">External research income.</span></li><li class="leaf"><b>Industry partnerships</b><span class="d">Collaboration that funds research and links to jobs.</span></li><li class="leaf"><b>Full cost recovery</b><span class="d">Whether grants cover true cost.</span></li></ul></li><li class="lever cost"><div class="node"><div class="lh"><span class="ln"><i class="lno">Lever 3</i><b>Financial health</b></span><span class="badge cost">▼ Mainly cost</span></div></div><ul class="branch"><li class="leaf"><b>Endowment returns</b><span class="d">Investment performance.</span></li><li class="leaf"><b>Cost per student</b><span class="d">Efficiency of delivery.</span></li><li class="leaf"><b>Debt service</b><span class="d">Repayments on capital projects.</span></li></ul></li></ul><p class="q"><b>Critical questions</b> How dependent are we on tuition or a single funding source? Is research funding covering its true cost?</p></div></details>
<details class="bu" open><summary><span class="bn">4</span><span class="bt">Student Services &amp; Outcomes</span><span class="badge rev">BU leans revenue</span><span class="sm">2 mainly revenue, 0 mainly cost, 1 both</span></summary><div class="body"><ul class="branch root"><li class="lever rev"><div class="node"><div class="lh"><span class="ln"><i class="lno">Lever 1</i><b>Progression</b></span><span class="badge rev">▲ Mainly revenue</span></div></div><ul class="branch"><li class="leaf"><b>Retention</b><span class="d">Students continuing through their program.</span></li><li class="leaf"><b>Graduation rate</b><span class="d">Share who complete.</span></li><li class="leaf"><b>Time to completion</b><span class="d">Speed of graduating.</span></li></ul></li><li class="lever rev"><div class="node"><div class="lh"><span class="ln"><i class="lno">Lever 2</i><b>Outcomes</b></span><span class="badge rev">▲ Mainly revenue</span></div></div><ul class="branch"><li class="leaf"><b>Graduate employment</b><span class="d">Share employed after graduation.</span></li><li class="leaf"><b>Salary outcomes</b><span class="d">Earnings that justify the price paid.</span></li><li class="leaf"><b>Employer relationships</b><span class="d">Links that support placement.</span></li></ul></li><li class="lever bal"><div class="node"><div class="lh"><span class="ln"><i class="lno">Lever 3</i><b>Student experience</b></span><span class="badge bal">◆ Both</span></div></div><ul class="branch"><li class="leaf"><b>Satisfaction</b><span class="d">How students rate their experience.</span></li><li class="leaf"><b>Wellbeing and support usage</b><span class="d">Use and quality of counselling and advising.</span></li><li class="leaf"><b>Alumni engagement</b><span class="d">Long-term connection and giving.</span></li></ul></li></ul><p class="q"><b>Critical questions</b> Why do students drop out? Do graduates get jobs that justify what they pay?</p></div></details>
<details class="bu" open><summary><span class="bn">5</span><span class="bt">Corporate Enablers (Faculty &amp; Staff, IT, Facilities, Compliance)</span><span class="badge cost">BU leans cost</span><span class="sm">1 mainly revenue, 2 mainly cost, 0 both</span></summary><div class="body"><ul class="branch root"><li class="lever cost"><div class="node"><div class="lh"><span class="ln"><i class="lno">Lever 1</i><b>People</b></span><span class="badge cost">▼ Mainly cost</span></div></div><ul class="branch"><li class="leaf"><b>Faculty recruitment and retention</b><span class="d">Attracting and keeping academic talent.</span></li><li class="leaf"><b>Staff productivity</b><span class="d">Efficiency of administration.</span></li><li class="leaf"><b>Workload balance</b><span class="d">Teaching, research and admin demands on staff.</span></li></ul></li><li class="lever cost"><div class="node"><div class="lh"><span class="ln"><i class="lno">Lever 2</i><b>Technology and facilities</b></span><span class="badge cost">▼ Mainly cost</span></div></div><ul class="branch"><li class="leaf"><b>Digital infrastructure</b><span class="d">Learning and administrative systems.</span></li><li class="leaf"><b>Data systems</b><span class="d">Information for decisions.</span></li><li class="leaf"><b>Campus utilization</b><span class="d">Use of buildings and space.</span></li></ul></li><li class="lever rev"><div class="node"><div class="lh"><span class="ln"><i class="lno">Lever 3</i><b>Standing</b></span><span class="badge rev">▲ Mainly revenue</span></div></div><ul class="branch"><li class="leaf"><b>Accreditation</b><span class="d">Standing that affects funding and enrollment.</span></li><li class="leaf"><b>Rankings</b><span class="d">Reputation signals that drive demand.</span></li><li class="leaf"><b>Regulatory reporting</b><span class="d">Meeting compliance requirements.</span></li></ul></li></ul><p class="q"><b>Critical questions</b> Is administrative growth outpacing teaching investment? Are we maintaining accreditation and rankings standards?</p></div></details>
