<h2>🤖 Data &amp; AI Projects (Cross-Industry)</h2>
<p class="logic"><span class="lbl">How the business flows</span><span class="chain"><span class="step">Choose the right problem</span><span class="step">Get the data</span><span class="step">Build the model</span><span class="step">Deploy and run it</span><span class="step">Govern and enable</span></span></p>
<details class="bu" open><summary><span class="bn">1</span><span class="bt">Use Case Strategy &amp; Business Value</span><span class="badge rev">BU leans revenue</span><span class="sm">1 mainly revenue, 0 mainly cost, 2 both</span></summary><div class="body"><ul class="branch root"><li class="lever bal"><div class="node"><div class="lh"><span class="ln"><i class="lno">Lever 1</i><b>Prioritization</b></span><span class="badge bal">◆ Both</span></div></div><ul class="branch"><li class="leaf"><b>Use case selection</b><span class="d">Ranking ideas by impact vs feasibility.</span></li><li class="leaf"><b>Strategic alignment</b><span class="d">Tie to business strategy.</span></li><li class="leaf"><b>KPI linkage</b><span class="d">Connection to metrics the business tracks.</span></li></ul></li><li class="lever rev"><div class="node"><div class="lh"><span class="ln"><i class="lno">Lever 2</i><b>Value capture</b></span><span class="badge rev">▲ Mainly revenue</span></div></div><ul class="branch"><li class="leaf"><b>Uplift or saving per use case</b><span class="d">Expected revenue gain or cost reduction.</span></li><li class="leaf"><b>Business owner adoption</b><span class="d">A named owner who takes responsibility for the benefit.</span></li><li class="leaf"><b>Benefit tracking</b><span class="d">Confirming value is realized after launch.</span></li></ul></li><li class="lever bal"><div class="node"><div class="lh"><span class="ln"><i class="lno">Lever 3</i><b>Portfolio</b></span><span class="badge bal">◆ Both</span></div></div><ul class="branch"><li class="leaf"><b>Quick wins vs long-term bets</b><span class="d">Balancing near-term value and strategic capability.</span></li><li class="leaf"><b>Build, buy or partner</b><span class="d">How capability is sourced.</span></li><li class="leaf"><b>Sequencing</b><span class="d">Ordering projects so early work supports later ones.</span></li></ul></li></ul><p class="q"><b>Critical questions</b> Which use cases move a P&amp;L line, not just a pilot? Who owns the benefit once the model is live?</p></div></details>
<details class="bu" open><summary><span class="bn">2</span><span class="bt">Data Foundation &amp; Engineering</span><span class="badge cost">BU leans cost</span><span class="sm">0 mainly revenue, 2 mainly cost, 1 both</span></summary><div class="body"><ul class="branch root"><li class="lever cost"><div class="node"><div class="lh"><span class="ln"><i class="lno">Lever 1</i><b>Availability</b></span><span class="badge cost">▼ Mainly cost</span></div></div><ul class="branch"><li class="leaf"><b>Data coverage</b><span class="d">Whether the needed data exists.</span></li><li class="leaf"><b>System integration</b><span class="d">Bringing data together across systems.</span></li><li class="leaf"><b>Access</b><span class="d">How easily teams can use the data.</span></li></ul></li><li class="lever bal"><div class="node"><div class="lh"><span class="ln"><i class="lno">Lever 2</i><b>Quality</b></span><span class="badge bal">◆ Both</span></div></div><ul class="branch"><li class="leaf"><b>Accuracy</b><span class="d">Whether data is correct.</span></li><li class="leaf"><b>Completeness and freshness</b><span class="d">Gaps and how current data is.</span></li><li class="leaf"><b>Labelling quality</b><span class="d">Correct labels for supervised learning.</span></li></ul></li><li class="lever cost"><div class="node"><div class="lh"><span class="ln"><i class="lno">Lever 3</i><b>Architecture</b></span><span class="badge cost">▼ Mainly cost</span></div></div><ul class="branch"><li class="leaf"><b>Pipeline reliability</b><span class="d">Stable, repeatable data flow.</span></li><li class="leaf"><b>Reuse of data assets</b><span class="d">Avoiding rebuilding the same pipelines per project.</span></li><li class="leaf"><b>Storage and processing scalability</b><span class="d">Warehouse or lake capacity that grows with use.</span></li></ul></li></ul><p class="q"><b>Critical questions</b> Is the data good enough to support the use case today? Are we rebuilding the same pipelines for each project?</p></div></details>
<details class="bu" open><summary><span class="bn">3</span><span class="bt">Model Development &amp; Experimentation</span><span class="badge cost">BU leans cost</span><span class="sm">1 mainly revenue, 2 mainly cost, 0 both</span></summary><div class="body"><ul class="branch root"><li class="lever rev"><div class="node"><div class="lh"><span class="ln"><i class="lno">Lever 1</i><b>Performance</b></span><span class="badge rev">▲ Mainly revenue</span></div></div><ul class="branch"><li class="leaf"><b>Accuracy, precision and recall</b><span class="d">Measures against the business metric.</span></li><li class="leaf"><b>Fit to the business metric</b><span class="d">Whether the model optimizes what actually matters.</span></li><li class="leaf"><b>Evaluation and testing</b><span class="d">Rigor of validation before release.</span></li></ul></li><li class="lever cost"><div class="node"><div class="lh"><span class="ln"><i class="lno">Lever 2</i><b>Development speed</b></span><span class="badge cost">▼ Mainly cost</span></div></div><ul class="branch"><li class="leaf"><b>Experiment velocity</b><span class="d">Speed of testing ideas.</span></li><li class="leaf"><b>Pretrained and foundation model reuse</b><span class="d">Starting from existing models to save time and cost.</span></li><li class="leaf"><b>Tooling</b><span class="d">Platforms that speed up development.</span></li></ul></li><li class="lever cost"><div class="node"><div class="lh"><span class="ln"><i class="lno">Lever 3</i><b>Approach choice</b></span><span class="badge cost">▼ Mainly cost</span></div></div><ul class="branch"><li class="leaf"><b>Custom vs fine-tune vs off-the-shelf</b><span class="d">Balancing control, cost and speed.</span></li><li class="leaf"><b>Complexity vs explainability</b><span class="d">Trade-off between power and transparency.</span></li><li class="leaf"><b>Compute discipline</b><span class="d">Managing training and experimentation cost.</span></li></ul></li></ul><p class="q"><b>Critical questions</b> Is a simpler model good enough for the decision? Does model accuracy translate into business value?</p></div></details>
<details class="bu" open><summary><span class="bn">4</span><span class="bt">Deployment, Operations &amp; Adoption</span><span class="badge bal">BU is even</span><span class="sm">1 mainly revenue, 1 mainly cost, 1 both</span></summary><div class="body"><ul class="branch root"><li class="lever rev"><div class="node"><div class="lh"><span class="ln"><i class="lno">Lever 1</i><b>Productionization</b></span><span class="badge rev">▲ Mainly revenue</span></div></div><ul class="branch"><li class="leaf"><b>Time to production</b><span class="d">Speed from prototype to live.</span></li><li class="leaf"><b>Workflow integration</b><span class="d">Fit within existing systems and processes.</span></li><li class="leaf"><b>Operations handover</b><span class="d">Clear ownership between build and run teams.</span></li></ul></li><li class="lever cost"><div class="node"><div class="lh"><span class="ln"><i class="lno">Lever 2</i><b>Reliability</b></span><span class="badge cost">▼ Mainly cost</span></div></div><ul class="branch"><li class="leaf"><b>Uptime and latency</b><span class="d">Reliability of the live service.</span></li><li class="leaf"><b>Drift monitoring</b><span class="d">Detecting degradation in model performance.</span></li><li class="leaf"><b>Retraining cadence</b><span class="d">Refreshing models as data changes.</span></li></ul></li><li class="lever bal"><div class="node"><div class="lh"><span class="ln"><i class="lno">Lever 3</i><b>Adoption</b></span><span class="badge bal">◆ Both</span></div></div><ul class="branch"><li class="leaf"><b>User trust and usage</b><span class="d">Whether people rely on the output.</span></li><li class="leaf"><b>Change management</b><span class="d">Training and process redesign.</span></li><li class="leaf"><b>Run cost</b><span class="d">Inference and hosting cost at scale.</span></li></ul></li></ul><p class="q"><b>Critical questions</b> Why do most pilots fail to reach production? Are users actually changing how they work because of the model?</p></div></details>
<details class="bu" open><summary><span class="bn">5</span><span class="bt">Governance, Risk &amp; Enablers (Talent, Security, Compliance)</span><span class="badge cost">BU leans cost</span><span class="sm">0 mainly revenue, 2 mainly cost, 1 both</span></summary><div class="body"><ul class="branch root"><li class="lever bal"><div class="node"><div class="lh"><span class="ln"><i class="lno">Lever 1</i><b>Responsible AI</b></span><span class="badge bal">◆ Both</span></div></div><ul class="branch"><li class="leaf"><b>Bias and fairness testing</b><span class="d">Checking outputs across groups.</span></li><li class="leaf"><b>Explainability</b><span class="d">Ability to justify decisions.</span></li><li class="leaf"><b>Human oversight</b><span class="d">Review points for high-stakes outputs.</span></li></ul></li><li class="lever cost"><div class="node"><div class="lh"><span class="ln"><i class="lno">Lever 2</i><b>Protection and compliance</b></span><span class="badge cost">▼ Mainly cost</span></div></div><ul class="branch"><li class="leaf"><b>Privacy and security</b><span class="d">Access controls and data protection.</span></li><li class="leaf"><b>Regulatory compliance</b><span class="d">Meeting AI and data regulation.</span></li><li class="leaf"><b>IP and model ownership</b><span class="d">Clarity over who owns models and outputs.</span></li></ul></li><li class="lever cost"><div class="node"><div class="lh"><span class="ln"><i class="lno">Lever 3</i><b>Capability</b></span><span class="badge cost">▼ Mainly cost</span></div></div><ul class="branch"><li class="leaf"><b>Talent attraction and retention</b><span class="d">Keeping scarce AI skills.</span></li><li class="leaf"><b>Operating model</b><span class="d">Central vs embedded teams.</span></li><li class="leaf"><b>Upskilling</b><span class="d">Building AI literacy across the business.</span></li></ul></li></ul><p class="q"><b>Critical questions</b> What is the cost of one biased, leaked or wrong model output? Can we attract and keep the talent needed to run this at scale?</p></div></details>
</section>
